  "body": "## Change and mathematical scope\n\n**Replacement-interface result, with priced instances on every committed R439\ntarget-basis word. No new \u03ba, and the bit side does not bind.** This adds one\nregistered package,\n[`research/r439-deferred-target-basis-seed06/`](research/r439-deferred-target-basis-seed06/README.md).\nNo selected record, supplier, pinned file or `upstream/` file changes.\n\n**The contract (H5-tw).** Every contract on main keeps the bit supplier's H5\n(`V = I`). That includes PR1194's semantic D and PR1868's twisted helpers.\n\n- **The lemma.** Let D be frame-zero and source-free, with operator\n  `(x, y, h) -> (x, R y + N h, T h)`, and keep H1, H3 and a z-only full-frame C.\n  Then the dirty boundary `(x, y, h) -> (x, y + x, h)` holds **if and only if**\n  `V R = I`, `J = I`, `V N = K'T` and `C U'(I \u2295 T) = I`, where V is the target\n  block of `(A, scatter, B)`.\n- **What it relaxes.** H5 together with the H2 target clause.\n- **What it keeps.** D-shape and cleanup.\n- **What it generalizes.** K becomes `V N = K'T`.\n- **Proof.** The proof (`PROOF.md` \u00a71\u20132) is block algebra. It was also checked\n  on 4,000 random small F2 words during review.\n\n**The construction (`R = E`, `V = E\u207b\u00b9`).** Every PR915-lineage word prepares a\ntarget basis E in D and undoes it at the end of D. Here the 306 undo gates\n(307 on PR1040/PR1449) move, unchanged, to the start of B. They stay at frame 0,\nbefore any target climbs. The 9-column scatter is then listed in the target\nbasis as `E S`.\n\n- **Bridge.** Between the deferred undo and its new position, the targets hold\n  `E\u00b7(original)` at frame 0, and no gate reads them. The bridge replays both\n  words cut by cut. We argue that it needs no new physical premise, by inherited\n  H3 and common-label realization. Unlike PR1194's prefix-only substitution,\n  the twisted window runs through A and the scatter.\n- **Price.** The scatter goes 527 \u2192 97. Frame paths, MOVE records and the paid\n  profile `{1:1323, 2:1342, 3:79, 4:44, 5:102, 6:11, 7:19}` (rank mass 5,129)\n  are unchanged.\n- **Precision.** F is unchanged and B falls. No guard bit rises.\n- **Owner checker.** The unchanged `xcheck_p.py` makes exactly `H5_V_identity`\n  newly false.\n\n**Census of every committed lineage word** (19 distinct words at base `c6765481`,\ncomplete local ADDs):\n\n| word | base | deferred | B (exporter) | bits |\n|---|---:|---:|---|---|\n| PR915 | 13,208 | 12,778 | 9,534,616 \u2192 8,742,940 | 100/189 \u2192 99/189 |\n| PR967 | 11,783 | 11,353 | 10,394,084 \u2192 9,602,408 | 102/192 \u2192 101/192 |\n| PR1040 | 11,780 | 11,348 (\u2212432) | 10,394,084 \u2192 9,602,408 | 102/192 \u2192 101/192 |\n| PR1062 | 11,500 | 11,070 | 5,911,840 \u2192 5,024,524 | 95/182 \u2192 95/181 |\n| PR1122 | 10,652 | 10,222 | 3,910,388 \u2192 2,996,128 | 92/176 \u2192 91/174 |\n| PR1188 | 10,492 | 10,062 | 3,758,418 \u2192 2,825,146 | 91/175 \u2192 91/173 |\n| PR1709 | 11,488 | 11,058 | 5,921,344 \u2192 5,034,028 | 96/182 \u2192 95/181 |\n| PR1868 absorbed PR1188 (T \u2260 I) | 10,489 | **10,059** | 3,748,680 \u2192 2,816,834 | 91/175 \u2192 91/173 |\n| \u2026 11 more (PR926, PR941, PR941-floor, PR965, PR1047, PR1062-composition, PR1062-pair-control, PR1208, PR1449, PR1543, PR1868-1062) | | \u2212430 each | | |\n\n- PR941's floor-calibration word misses the nine-stage guard at 193 bits, and its\n  deferred word meets it at 192.\n- Eight outside words (PR555/PR589 and others) have no target basis, so deferral\n  is vacuous on them.\n\n**Maximality and refinement.**\n\n- **Maximality.** It is proved under fixed ordered frame paths.\n  - The 111 targets' nonzero frame sets are pairwise disjoint.\n  - None of the 585 (undo gate, B write) absorption pairs is frame-legal.\n  - Full deferral attains the minimum over prefix splits of the literal undo\n    order.\n  - If frame paths may change, the package reports loose and strict counts of\n    possible partners (up to 58, and up to 7 by the strictest criterion), so the\n    claim is scoped.\n- **Order-ideal refinement.** Allowing commuting reorders, keeping the order ideal\n  {31, 51, 52} before the scatter gives 94. It goes through the same full checks.\n  The results are PR1062 11,067, PR1188 10,059, PR1868-absorbed PR1188 **10,056**,\n  and PR1040 11,345. It was found by exhaustive search over ideals of size \u2264 4\n  plus greedy descent, so it is not claimed optimal.\n- **Selected-word heuristic.** On PR589, a minimum-spanning-tree scatter basis G\n  gives 24,305 \u2192 24,190 (scatter 527 \u2192 412). It is labelled heuristic. Owner flags\n  H2, H5 and K become false there, and B rises slightly.\n\n**Not run.**\n\n- The native 5/9/11-stage C++ replay (no Boost here; PR1902's harness could take\n  it).\n- Hosted emission, for example PR1806's PR1122 invoice on the deferred word.\n- The undo moves from exporter phase 1 (D) to phase 4 (B). Any phase-specific\n  expectation in the native tools is unchecked.\n\n## Task and overlap\n\n- **Base and track.** Base `c6765481`. Seed 6 \u2192 bit supplier, card\n  `bit-helper-contract` (scope key `3475f46c8358c6a9211b`), scope **changed**.\n  The card asks for an H2/K replacement for a helper operation. This package\n  also relaxes H5, which the card keeps, and its object is the target-basis\n  block.\n- **Nearest construction.** PR1704 (Ross Richardson, merged), a two-copy\n  scatter, 527 \u2192 407 under a copied-workspace contract. It is a different\n  mechanism, and not additive: both rewrite the same block.\n- **Target-basis packages.** PR794 (open), PR915 and the r420/r439 target-basis\n  packages all keep `E\u207b\u00b9` inside D.\n- **Contrasting deferral results.** PR1580/PR1592 defer helper restorations to\n  the end; this package defers a target-basis undo.\n- **Overlap searches.** I searched PRs and Discussions for scatter, target basis,\n  H5, V_identity, deferred undo, twisted target, 10,062, 11,070 and 10,059,\n  including Discussion #1166 and PRs through #2099. None defers the target-basis\n  undo or lists the scatter in the target basis.\n\n## Validation\n\n```sh\npython3 scripts/research_package.py --package research/r439-deferred-target-basis-seed06 --check-only\npython3.12 scripts/research_package.py --package research/r439-deferred-target-basis-seed06\n```\n\n`verify.py` uses only the standard library and takes about 65 s. Its checks\nraise `ValueError`, and it is registered plain and under `-O`.\n\n**Inputs.** All 29 inputs and 2 provenance files are pinned by SHA-256 and git blob. The owner checker\nand exporter run from the verified bytes.\n\n**Per word, the verifier:**\n- re-derives the deferral;\n- replays the literal 661-column COPY/ERASE dirty boundary forward and reverse;\n- checks frame paths, MOVE records, the exporter paid profile and both precision\n  guards, the owner-flag delta, the four H5-tw equations exactly, the per-cut\n  bridge and the maximality census.\n\nIt also rebuilds the committed PR1062 and PR1188 candidates byte for byte, and\nadds `--census-scan`, which found 27 R439 words: 27 listed, 0 unlisted.\n\n**33 controls, all rejected:**\n- the old S listing;\n- the undo moved after B[0];\n- a dropped undo gate;\n- preparation-order undo;\n- non-commuting swaps;\n- a wrong `E S` row;\n- a corrupted pin;\n- the bridge on blind or old-S or swapped words;\n- an owner delta on (base, base);\n- legal frame raises against paths and against the profile;\n- the maximality census with the wrong base;\n- the precision guard on the 193-bit floor word.\n\nA 26-mutant run against the verifier caught 20. The 6 survivors are listed in\nthe README: two call-site removals of pinned outputs, an equivalent `<`/`<=`\nmutant, two redundant pins, and a gzip mtime change. Tested on Python 3.12.15\nand 3.14.8.\n\n**Pre-PR review.** Three lenses (proof, verifier, claims) returned\nship-with-fixes, and all fixes are applied:\n- The proof lens confirmed the lemma and its converse and found the order-ideal\n  refinement.\n- The verifier lens independently reproduced 10,492 \u2192 10,062 byte for byte. It\n  found that the bridge rebuilt the deferred side from the base word, which is\n  now fixed, and found missing check-level controls, now 33.\n- The claims lens found that the scope label should be \"changed\", that the\n  wording implied a public pre-claim, and that the PR794/PR716/#476/PR686 credits\n  were missing. All are fixed.\n\n## Credit\n\n- **Target-basis lineage:**\n  - Gareth Davidson / bitplane (PR915, the E block deferred here; PR926, PR941,\n    PR1122, PR1188);\n  - commdata2338 (PR794);\n  - Scott Woolsey Biggart (PR713);\n  - Sagar Thakrar (PR716);\n  - Dugongue (#476/#478).\n- **Lineage words:**\n  - Sricharan Vagvala (PR967);\n  - Ross Richardson (PR923, PR965, PR936);\n  - Aaron Wang / navinor (PR1015, PR1127);\n  - Sagar Thakrar (PR1062, PR1868);\n  - woklerx (PR1040, PR1047);\n  - Hanson Sun / bbMisk (PR1449, PR1221, PR1902);\n  - ToikY (PR1543, PR1208);\n  - Cinna Davis / 1337isnot1337 (PR1709);\n  - DreamingOfClouds (PR589, PR545).\n- **Interface and checkers:**\n  - eumemic (PR543 H1\u2013H5 lemma, PR555, `xcheck_p.py`);\n  - Zhihao Chen (PR425);\n  - Mikhail R. Gadelha (PR686);\n  - woklerx (PR1194);\n  - Arham Tahir (PR1311);\n  - Dylan Crow (exporter).\n- **Nearest construction:** Ross Richardson (PR1704).\n\nAI disclosure: prepared by Sagar Thakrar with substantial Anthropic Claude\nassistance, including explorer, judge, builder and reviewer subagents. No\nindependent human review. New work is Apache-2.0.\n\n## Open next questions\n\n1. Native 5/9/11-stage replay of the deferred words, for example with PR1902's\n   harness.\n2. Larger order ideals, or a proof that 94 is optimal over commutation-closed\n   splits.\n3. Re-running PR794's greedy target-basis search with the deferred objective,\n   which counts `E S` instead of S.\n4. Hosted invoice of the deferred PR1122 word via PR1806's route.\n5. An optimal scatter basis G on the selected PR589 word. The MST gives 412.\n6. Composition with the restored helper-shear descent on PR1188's star D. B's\n   drop frees nine-stage headroom, which is the descent's binding resource.\n",
